From 5899081a48c60df8d50eb7fc16a743693c671497 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:35:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/27] esp32s3: LCD_CAM's LCD side (8080/i80 parallel
 displays)

LCD_CAM in i80 mode, as ESP-IDF's esp_lcd i80 driver uses it: a transaction
(USER.START) sends the command phase (CMD_VAL, one or two bytes), sets D/C for
the dummy phase, then sends data from the GDMA: as long as the descriptors say
(ALWAYS_OUT) or CYCLELEN cycles of one or two bytes. 8BITS_ORDER swaps byte
pairs, BIT_ORDER reverses bits. D/C follows MISC's CD_*_SET bits against its
idle level. The bus is an SSI bus, "lcd", so the MIPI DBI panels work on it as
on SPI; CS and D/C are GPIO matrix signals 132 and 153. TRANS_DONE raises the
LCD_CAM interrupt. The RGB mode isn't modelled (logged).

esp_gdma_out_chain_length() gives a channel's descriptor chain's length up to
its EOF, for ALWAYS_OUT.

Tested with esp32s3-lcd-cam-test, and the T-Display-S3's factory firmware (its
LVGL UI on a 170x320 ST7789).
